  "note": "reviewed is false and MUST stay false until a qualified reviewer has verified every entry against the operator's own source. While it is false Half names no line at all and 6a's generic wording stands — that is deliberate. These entries were written from memory: they are the right shape and their truth is unverified, and a helpline number that is right in shape and wrong in fact is the most dangerous thing in this repository. The crisis subsystem's clinical review (companion build requirement 6) covers this file, not only the code that reads it. Do not add regions from memory: that increases the surface without increasing the truth.",
  "shape": "regions maps a region key the main themselves told Half to an ordered list of lines; order is the curator's judgement and is preserved. aliases maps what a person actually calls a place to one of those keys. reach is whatever the person actually does — a short code, a number, an instruction to text a word somewhere — because the shapes differ by country and a schema that modelled them would drop the ones it had not met. No value may contain a newline, a control character, ' - ' with spaces around an em dash, or ' . ' with spaces around a middle dot: those are the separators a rendered row is joined from. No region is privileged; Half has no default.",
